%N A401358 Irregular triangle read by rows: row n lists the arithmetic means of the outermost pairs of primes in the interval [prime(n)^2, prime(n+1)^2].
%C A401358 The arithmetic mean of a pair of primes (p, q) is defined as (p + q)/2. The primes in the interval are sorted in ascending order and paired from the outermost to the innermost. If the total number of primes in the interval is odd, the median prime is paired with itself. The number of terms in row n is ceiling(A050216(n)/2), where A050216(n) is the number of primes in the interval [prime(n)^2, prime(n+1)^2].
%e A401358 For n = 2, the interval is [3^2, 5^2] = [9, 25]. The primes are {11, 13, 17, 19, 23}. The outer pairs are (11, 23) and (13, 19), and the median prime 17 is paired with itself. Their means are 17, 16, and 17. Thus, row 2 is 17, 16, 17.
%e A401358 For n = 3, the interval is [5^2, 7^2] = [25, 49]. The primes in this interval are {29, 31, 37, 41, 43, 47}. Pairing them from the outside in gives (29, 47), (31, 43), and (37, 41). Their arithmetic means are 38, 37, and 39. Thus, row 3 is 38, 37, 39.
%o A401358 (Python)
%o A401358 from sympy import isprime, prime
%o A401358 def row(n):
%o A401358     p1, p2 = prime(n), prime(n + 1)
%o A401358     q = [x for x in range(p1**2, p2**2 + 1) if isprime(x)]
%o A401358     m = len(q)
%o A401358     return [(q[i] + q[m - 1 - i]) // 2 for i in range((m + 1) // 2)]
%o A401358 # Print the flattened sequence
%o A401358 seq = []
%o A401358 for n in range(1, 10):
%o A401358     seq.extend(row(n))
%o A401358 print(seq)
%Y A401358 Cf. A000040, A050216.
%K A401358 nonn,tabf,easy,new
%O A401358 1,1
